        "by": "FarhanAliRaza",
        "outdated": false,
        "first_comment": "If the env var is not set and no config is cached, the flag falls back to `False` with no warning. Every public method then becomes an event handler again. This happens for any entry point other than "
      },
      {
        "by": "FarhanAliRaza",
        "outdated": false,
        "first_comment": "The exported env var also wins over later `rxconfig.py` edits, because `update_from_env` applies `REFLEX_*` over the file values. In dev, the worker reloads with the value from startup.\n\nRepro: start "
      },
      {
        "by": "FarhanAliRaza",
        "outdated": false,
        "first_comment": "This check runs only when a trigger is compiled. The runtime paths through `Event.from_event_type` and `fix_events` do not call it. Both cases below work in implicit mode, so users who migrate will hi"
      },
      {
        "by": "FarhanAliRaza",
        "outdated": false,
        "first_comment": "A decorator without `functools.wraps` on top of `@rx.event` loses this marker. So the method silently stops being an event handler:\n\n```python\ndef require_login(f):\n    def inner(self, *a, **k):\n     "
      },
      {
        "by": "FarhanAliRaza",
        "outdated": false,
        "first_comment": "This `setattr` runs in the default mode too. So `rx.event(x)` now raises for any `x` without a `__dict__`:\n\n```python\nrx.event(Obj().m)\n# AttributeError: 'method' object has no attribute '_rx_event' a"
      },
      {
        "by": "FarhanAliRaza",
        "outdated": false,
        "first_comment": "These two markers are internal, but adding them to `EventNamespace` makes them public as `rx.event.EVENT_MARKER` and `rx.event.UNDECORATED_STATE_METHOD_MARKER`. `reflex/state.py` imports them from `re"
      }
    ]
